"""
The installer on the Nothing Liquid USB: puts Arch Linux and Nothing Liquid on
a computer, next to Windows or on a whole disk, for someone who has never used
Linux. It runs as root, full screen in the cage kiosk the USB starts
(iso/airootfs/usr/local/bin/nothing-liquid-live-session); live/install-system.sh
does the work, and the desktop finishes setting itself up at the first start.

  nothing-liquid-live          the real thing (on the USB)
  nothing-liquid-live --demo   every screen, with a made-up Windows laptop; no
                               disk is touched (try it on any computer)

A different keyboard layout restarts the kiosk with it (exit code 3).
"""

